  "worked_solution": "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows:\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}+0x-5\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x-10 \\\\  & 2x+10\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,4{x}^{2}+0x-5} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{2}+20x}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-20x-5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,20x-100}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,95\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $2x-10\\,$ and $\\,-20x-100.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
